              highlighted: ["angB","angE"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Cut {BA}, {BC}, {ED}, and {EF} off equal to one another,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC","DE","EF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.3" }] },
            { text: "and join {AD}, {CF}, {BE}, {AC}, and {DF}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AD","CF","BE","AC","DF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "CF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "AC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "DF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {BA} equals and is parallel to {ED}, therefore {AD} also equals and is parallel to {BE}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AB","DE","AD","BE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "joining equal parallels", ref: "I.33" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason {CF} also equals and is parallel to {BE}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BC","EF","CF","BE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "joining equal parallels", ref: "I.33" }] },
            { text: "Therefore each of the straight lines {AD} and {CF} equals and is parallel to {BE}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AD","CF","BE"] },
            { text: "But straight lines which are parallel to the same straight line",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AD","CF","BE"] },
            { text: "and are not in the same plane with it are parallel to one another,",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AD","CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "parallels to one line, not in one plane", ref: "XI.9" }] },
            { text: "therefore {AD} is parallel and equal to {CF}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AD","CF"] },
            { text: "And {AC} and {DF} join them, therefore {AC} also equals and is parallel to {DF}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AC","DF","AD","CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "joining equal parallels", ref: "I.33" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the two sides {AB} and {BC} equal the two sides {DE} and {EF},",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC","DE","EF"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "ABC", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "DEF", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and the base {AC} equals the base {DF},",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: ["AC","DF"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {ABC|angB} equals the angle {DEF|angE}.",
              visible: TRI.concat(["angB","angE"]),
              highlighted: ["angB","angE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "three sides equal", ref: "I.8" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, if two straight lines meeting one another",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "are parallel to two straight lines meeting one another not in the same plane,",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: ["DE","EF"] },
            { text: "then they contain equal angles.",
              visible: TRI.concat(["angB","angE"]),
              highlighted: ["angB","angE"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.10") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.3":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "I.8":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI8/",
        "I.33":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI33/",
        "XI.9":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI9/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Cut {BA}, {BC}, {ED}, and {EF} off equal to one another, and join {AD}, {CF}, {BE}, {AC}, and {DF}. [!just I.3]

Now, since {BA} equals and is parallel to {ED}, therefore {AD} also equals and is parallel to {BE}. For the same reason {CF} also equals and is parallel to {BE}. [!just I.33]

Therefore each of the straight lines {AD} and {CF} equals and is parallel to {BE}. But straight lines which are parallel to the same straight line and are not in the same plane with it are parallel to one another, therefore {AD} is parallel and equal to {CF}. [!just XI.9]

And {AC} and {DF} join them, therefore {AC} also equals and is parallel to {DF}. [!just I.33]

Now, since the two sides {AB} and {BC} equal the two sides {DE} and {EF}, and the base {AC} equals the base {DF}, therefore the angle {ABC|angB} equals the angle {DEF|angE}. [!just I.8]

Therefore, *if two straight lines meeting one another are parallel to two straight lines meeting one another not in the same plane, then they contain equal angles.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

Of course it is necessary to be careful about in which directions the lines head. If one is changed to head into the opposite direction, then the angles won't be equal but supplementary instead.

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition is used in the proofs of propositions @XI.24 and @XII.3.
